            <div xml:id="d673">

                <pb facs="1014" n="882" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg882"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.512/421: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Mayer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-10-20T11:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 20,
                                1926—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 20—4:25
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>495. Your 234, October 16, 4 p.m. I am deferring action contemplated in third
                    paragraph my 485, October 16, 1 p.m., in view of <pb facs="1015" n="883"
                        xml:id="pg883"/> diplomatic body meeting called for this morning further to
                    discuss Canton tax situation in particular relation to certain instructions from
                    his Government which the British Minister, I understand, intends then to bring
                    to our attention.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mayer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
